findings.body:
**Treat a regular-file ancestor as deletion of its indexed descendants.**

When the index tracks `src/component/index.ts` and the working tree replaces `src/component/` with a regular file, the ancestor loop throws for `src/component/index.ts`. The copied index still lists that path, and the thrown error has no `code`, so the `catch` rethrows it. Capture fails for a valid working-tree change, and the replacement file is never captured.

A regular file at an ancestor path means the descendant does not exist on disk. Remove that descendant from the private index, as the existing `ENOENT` branch already does. Keep the rejection for symbolic-link ancestors. The `!isDirectory()` check still rejects them after this change.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
         for (let end = 1; end <= parents.length; end++) {
           const parent = await lstat(join(repo, ...parents.slice(0, end)));
+          if (parent.isFile()) throw new ReplacedAncestorError(path);
           if (!parent.isDirectory())
             throw new Error(`working-tree snapshot refuses non-directory ancestor: ${path}`);
         }
         info = await lstat(join(repo, path));
       } catch (error) {
-        if ((error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== 'ENOENT') throw error;
+        if (!(error instanceof ReplacedAncestorError) && (error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== 'ENOENT')
+          throw error;
         await git('update-index', '--force-remove', '--', path);
         continue;
       }
```

